cpp --predef=FILE [gcc's options] file.c -o file.i: the C preprocessor, the .i that gcc 16 -E writes, byte for byte, from the same options (a .S's .s too, -x assembler-with-cpp);
FILE: the target's predefined macros for each set of options (gcc -dM -E) and gcc's answers to __has_builtin and its kin (src/glibc/predef-<target>.txt);
libcpp's model: tokens with the white space before them, macro contexts with each token's virtual location, padding tokens,
the multiple-include optimization, and gcc's -E printer of line markers, newlines and columns (dev source: tools/dev/pp)
